# Loop restoration on real content — the answer is "LR is fine, the TRACKER is not"

host: Apple M4 Pro (8P+4E), macOS 26.5.2, 24 GB. Release (`lto=fat`), DEFAULT
features, NO `-C target-cpu=native`, NO `nice` on any timed run.
base: `main` @ 312dcc3, branch `fix/filmgrain-mt-479`.
reference: dav1d 1.5.4 (homebrew), in the SAME interleaved sweep, at BOTH
`--framedelay 1` (the tile-threading-only model we implement) and its shipping
default.
instrument: `scripts/perf/verify_gap_ivf.sh` + `examples/bench_ivf_limit` —
whole-process wall clock, one input file shared by both arms, run at two frame
counts per cell with `total = alpha + beta*frames` fitted so binary load, IVF
parse and decoder construction drop out. Per-cell frame counts (a 3-frame 4K
vector and a 557-frame QCIF one cannot share a pair).
raw: `lr_gap_ladder_2026-08-10.tsv.zst` (540 rows, 5 arms x 12 cells x 9 rounds),
`lr_tracker_isolation_2026-08-10.tsv.zst` (576 rows, 4 arms, thread ladder),
`feature_hunt_2026-08-10.tsv` (360 rows), `lr_selftime_t{1,8}_2026-08-10.txt`.

**LOAD TAG.** A sibling agent held one core with a `miri` run for the whole
sweep, so every row carries `foreign_max=1` and was committed under
`ALLOW_LOAD=1` / `measlock --load-ok`. **Absolute ms are inflated; read the
paired ratios.** Arms interleave back-to-back with a rotating order inside every
cell, so both sides of every ratio saw the same load. n=9 per cell, 0 discarded.

---

## 0. Two premises the task was given are FALSE. Checked first, on purpose.

* **"`looprestoration_arm.rs` has ZERO aarch64 intrinsics — the NEON tier is the
  scalar reference wearing a NEON name."** Not on `main` @ 312dcc3. The file is
  **1,812 lines with 61 distinct NEON intrinsics over 249 call sites**
  (`vaddq_s32` x32, `vdupq_n_s32` x26, `vld1q_s32` x23, `vqtbl4q_u8` x4, ...),
  `use core::arch::aarch64::*` at line 89, `#[arcane]` entry points, and
  `safe_unaligned_simd::aarch64`. That is MORE intrinsic sites than
  `ipred_arm.rs` (88), `cdef_arm.rs` (44) or `filmgrain_arm.rs` (30). The
  `perf/lr-neon-tier` branch (edb55a1) landed a real tier and it is on `main`.
* **"loop restoration has NEVER been measured."** It was, on 2026-08-08:
  `verify_compose3_2026-08-08.meta` §5, `verify_compose3_lrgap_2026-08-08.tsv`
  (216 rows). Everything below is a fresh, independent measurement on a wider
  ladder — but the prior record exists and is cited here rather than rediscovered.

**Verified: LR is active in 696 of 768 corpus vectors** (`md5_inventory
--activity --features __ablate`, re-run here — the number in the brief is right).
CDEF 727/768. **The other six activity columns are UNINSTRUMENTED**, not
inactive: only `itx`, `cdef` and `looprestoration` call `ablate::note()`. The
harness now says so out loud, because `loopfilter 0` reads as "never ran".

## 1. Is LR pathological? NO — it is our BEST subsystem against dav1d.

`RAV1D_INLOOP` / `--inloopfilters norestoration` on BOTH decoders, so LR's cost
is differenced out with one instrument instead of profiling ours and arguing
about theirs. Proof the two arms mean the same thing: at `all`,
`norestoration` and `none` our md5 is **byte-identical to dav1d 1.5.4's**
(`b90bd4a8…`, `ab33d6e6…`, `5fac46c2…` on `8-bit/data/00000647`, 4 frames).

  cell            bpc t |   ours  noLR  ourLR  LR% |  d1d  noLR  d1dLR  LR% | LR ratio  REST ratio
  3840x2160         8 1 | 160.50 145.50 15.00 9.3% | 40.50 32.50  8.00 19.8% |   1.88x      4.48x
  1920x1080        10 1 |   7.87   7.27  0.60 7.6% |  2.13  1.87  0.27 12.5% |   2.25x      3.89x
  640x360           8 1 |   3.08   3.00  0.08 2.4% |  0.47  0.45  0.02  5.3% |   3.00x      6.67x
  352x288 (I444)    8 1 |   5.20   5.09  0.11 2.2% |  0.80  0.75  0.05  6.5% |   2.17x      6.80x
  240x100           8 1 |   0.69   0.68  0.01 1.3% |  0.15  0.15  0.00  1.5% |   4.00x      4.66x

**LR is 1.9-2.3x of dav1d's LR at the two cells where it is big enough to
measure, while everything else in the decoder is 3.9-6.8x.** Its share of our
own wall clock is 9.3% at the worst cell (4K t=1) and 1.3-2.4% at the small
ones. Porting more of it cannot move the ratio: zeroing LR entirely at 4K t=1
takes 160.50 -> 145.50, i.e. 3.96x -> 3.59x.

**Do not port an LR kernel on this evidence.**

**Noise band on the LR RATIO — only the 4K cell resolves.** The ratio is a
quotient of two small differences, so it must be banded, not quoted as a point.
Differencing PER ROUND (both arms of both decoders from the same round, then
taking the median and range of the nine per-round quotients):

  cell            t | our LR ms/frame          d1d LR ms/frame        PAIRED LR ratio        n
  3840x2160  8b   1 | 15.50 [13.00..19.00]     7.50 [7.00..8.50]      **1.94x [1.75..2.57]** 9
  1920x1080 10b   1 |  0.60 [ 0.43.. 0.77]     0.27 [0.17..0.30]        2.50x [1.63..4.20]   9
  640x360    8b   1 |  0.12 [ 0.05.. 0.18]     0.02 [0.00..0.05]        3.00x [2.00..6.00]   7
  352x288 I444    1 |  0.10 [ 0.03.. 0.18]     0.05 [0.03..0.05]        2.33x [0.50..7.00]   9

**Only 4K 8bpc is resolvable: 1.75-2.57x.** Below it, LR's own cost is at the
1 ms timer floor (the 352x288 band crosses 1.0 and means nothing). Quote the 4K
band; treat the smaller cells' ratios as "same order, not resolved".

The load-bearing claim does NOT depend on that band. What decides "do not port"
is the SHARE, and that is measured directly: ours 4K t=1 [159.50..164.50] vs
noLR [144.50..148.00] are **disjoint**, so 9.3% is real, and the smaller cells'
shares are bounded above by 2.4%. A kernel worth 9.3% of the worst cell cannot
move a 4.0x ratio to 1.4x even if it became infinitely fast.

## 2. What IS pathological: real-content ratio 3.7x-46x, and thread scaling INVERTS

  cell            bpc |  t=1 ratio  t=8 ratio | ours t1 -> t8 | dav1d_fd1 t1 -> t8
  3840x2160         8 |     4.00x      8.20x  |  1.15x SLOWER |   0.56x faster
  1920x1080        10 |     3.67x     46.17x  |  3.54x SLOWER |   0.30x faster
  640x360           8 |     6.53x      7.78x  |  1.13x SLOWER |   0.95x
  352x288 (I444)    8 |     6.49x      9.61x  |  1.27x SLOWER |   0.87x
  240x100           8 |     4.65x      5.68x  |  1.38x SLOWER |   1.13x
  160x90           12 |     5.50x     11.00x  |  1.00x        |   1.00x

**Every LR-active cell in the ladder is slower at 8 threads than at 1**, ranges
disjoint at 5 of 6. It happens with LR OFF too (1.15x-3.75x), so it is not LR.
The 1.4x bar is met at NO cell on this content; the best cell in any sweep here
is all-intra 352x288 at **1.48x** (§4).

## 3. The cause, isolated: the DisjointMut borrow tracker. 93% of the wall at the worst cell.

`--features probe-untracked` ("tracking off, bounds checks untouched") is the
ceiling arm. Bit-identical output verified first (`fc5b4867…` on 318_tx_4x4 t=8,
`4b94c865…` on 00001147 t=8 — same md5 tracked and untracked).

  cell            bpc t |   ours  untracked  tracker share |  ours/d1d  untracked/d1d
  3840x2160         8 1 | 160.00     101.00          36.9% |     4.00x         2.52x
  3840x2160         8 8 | 184.50      70.50          61.8% |     8.20x         3.13x
  1920x1080        10 1 |   7.83       6.10          22.1% |     3.67x         2.86x
  1920x1080        10 4 |  16.10       2.27          85.9% |    24.15x         3.40x
  1920x1080        10 8 |  27.70       1.93        **93.0%**|    46.17x         3.22x
  640x360           8 8 |   3.50       2.10          40.0% |     7.78x         4.67x
  352x288 (I444)    8 8 |   6.60       3.37          48.9% |     9.61x         4.90x
  240x100           8 8 |   0.96       0.54          43.0% |     5.68x         3.23x
  160x90           12 8 |   1.38       1.00          27.3% |    11.00x         8.00x

Every one of those ours-vs-untracked pairs has **disjoint** per-round ranges.

**Thread scaling, tracked vs untracked (t=N / t=1):**

  1920x1080/10b   t=2  ours 1.13x  untracked 0.63x
                  t=4  ours 2.06x  untracked 0.37x
                  t=8  ours 3.54x  untracked 0.32x
  3840x2160/8b    t=8  ours 1.15x  untracked 0.70x
  640x360, 352x288, 240x100  t=8  ours 1.13-1.38x  untracked 0.99-1.11x

**The tracker converts a 3.1x speedup into a 3.5x slowdown.** Untracked scales;
tracked inverts. That is the whole inversion, at every cell.

`sample` self-time on `10-bit/issues/318_tx_4x4`, 25 s, `profile_ivf` with the
new `RAV1D_THREADS` knob (in-process ms/frame agreed with the two-point fit to
3.1-3.9%, so the instruments cross-check):

  t=1 (19,061 leaf samples)          t=8 (163,910 leaf samples)
  22.2% recon::mc<BitDepth16>        39.5% TinyLock::lock_slow
  11.3% _platform_memmove            39.3% __psynch_cvwait
   8.9% _platform_memset              5.3% BorrowTracker::add::<true>
   6.1% BorrowTracker::add::<true>    3.8% BorrowTracker::add::<false>
   6.1% BorrowTracker::add::<false>   2.3% BorrowTracker::add_wide::<false>
   3.9% recon::decode_coefs           2.2% BorrowTracker::add_contended::<true>
   2.3% lr_apply::lr_stripe           1.2% refmvs::load_tmvs
   ~5.8% all LR kernels combined      0.8% recon::mc  <- the actual pixel work
  ~13.2% all tracker symbols         ~55.3% all tracker symbols

