## 5. What this says to do next, ranked

1. **The tracker, on non-4K content.** It is 22-93% of our wall and it is the
   entire thread-scaling inversion. The brief lists "`TinyLock` backoff/yield —
   null, measured twice" as settled; **that null was measured on the 4K
   multi-tile grid, where `lock_slow` is not the top symbol. Here it is 39.5% of
   self time.** That is the contradicting profile the brief asks for before
   re-opening a measured null — the shape of the fix may still be different
   (fewer registrations, not a cheaper lock), but the target is not the same
   target that was refuted.
2. **Nothing in LR.** 1.9-2.3x, <=9.3% of wall, best-performing subsystem.
3. **intrabc's forced-scalar mc**, once a screen-content vector exists.
4. **Alpha/monochrome has one vector of corpus coverage.** Any I400 defect is
   near-invisible to the gate.
